   "user": "sasenchal",
   "message": "Symmetries under observation\n\nhttps://substack.com/profile/45219856-brent-borgers/note/c-331124053?r=4buhca&utm_medium=ios&utm_source=notes-share-action\n\nmonster group c.197k dimensions to spin and make a symmetry without hitting itself (minimum dim it needs to be rotated in) encodes a fundamental Fourier coefficient - a mathematical object that has enormous causal power in our world (essentially compressing that information to this single no. The j-invariant)\n\nIn obs theory this an object in the M domain (a high dimensional space with no associativety for us ie we can't imagine it)\n\nWhat we sample is in the world of its 5-d cousin - the J invariant and the second order 4d impacts of that constant (it impacts the outcome of scientific equations, ie physics)",
